      "observed": "C12 is a 2.2mF capacitor connected from BAT+ to GND, in an 0805 footprint.",
      "expected": "The specification identifies C12 as the 2.2 µF regulator input capacitor. Its value should be 2.2 µF, not 2.2 mF.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C12\") (value \"2.2mF\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C12\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C12\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C12 (2.2 µF) on BAT+→GND is the input cap"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C12 BAT+ 0 2.2m"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If built with the specified value, the input capacitance would be three orders of magnitude larger than intended and is not credible for the listed 0805 part. If the value is a unit-entry error and the intended part is 2.2 µF, the BOM/sourcing instruction is misleading; if actually implemented as 2.2 mF, it is an unsuitable part and could cause substantial startup and sourcing problems.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V and is connected across Display_Power_Switch and GND.",
      "expected": "The specification's EPD reference-circuit comparison lists C1 among the 1 µF/25 V capacitors; C1 should match that stated value and rating.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"9\") (name \"Display_Power_Switch\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The switched display rail has less bypass capacitance than the specification calls for, potentially worsening supply transients during display operation.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains a clear C12 value discrepancy: the netlist specifies 2.2 mF where the specification calls for 2.2 µF. C1 also differs from the value and rating stated in the EPD reference-circuit comparison."
}

